  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "present simple: affirmative for routines (I/he/she)",
      "title_form": "Presente simple: afirmativo para rutinas (I/he/she)",
      "title_target": "Present Simple: Affirmative for Routines (I/he/she)",
      "description_md_form": "El **present simple** se usa para hablar de **rutinas** y **hábitos** — cosas que haces **cada día**. Es el tiempo verbal de tu rutina de la mañana.\n\nPara la mayoría de las personas (I, you, we, they), el verbo se usa **sin cambios**:\n- `I wake up at seven.`\n- `They prepare breakfast.`\n\nPara **he, she, it**, el verbo lleva una **-s** al final:\n- `He wakes up at seven.`\n- `She packs her bag.`\n\n**Regla clave:** con he/she/it, el verbo cambia. Con I/you/we/they, no cambia.\n\nUsa **adverbios de secuencia** como `first` y `afterwards` para ordenar tus acciones: `First, I get up, and afterwards I have breakfast.`",
      "description_md_target": "The **present simple** is used to talk about **routines** and **habits** — things you do **every day**. It is the tense of your morning routine.\n\nFor most people (I, you, we, they), the verb is used **without changes**:\n- `I wake up at seven.`\n- `They prepare breakfast.`\n\nFor **he, she, it**, the verb takes an **-s** at the end:\n- `He wakes up at seven.`\n- `She packs her bag.`\n\n**Key rule:** with he/she/it, the verb changes. With I/you/we/they, it does not change.\n\nUse **sequence adverbs** like `first` and `afterwards` to order your actions: `First, I get up, and afterwards I have breakfast.`",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + verb (+ -s for he/she/it) + complement",
